Chapter: VecSized

 The sized-vector builtins had a registry row, a type and an emitter each and
 zero call sites, so nothing in the tree ever ran one. `vec-singleton` reached
 `__list_cons`, which extends the list it finds in `rsi` while
 `emit-helper-call-1` loads only `rdi`, and the general-protection fault that
 followed was invisible for the same reason: no test named these.

 One line per builtin, so a fault in one names itself rather than arriving as
 a silent absence.

 `vec-empty` is the only one of the five reached as a bare name rather than a
 call, so its rows are what hold the nullary-builtin route open: without it
 the name is emitted as a call to a symbol nothing defines and the chapter
 fails to compile at all rather than answering wrong.

 THE TWO LENGTH ROWS CANNOT CATCH THE OTHER HALF, and the two consuming rows
 below them are not redundant with anything. Measured against a compiler with
 the empty vector emitted as a literal 0: both length rows still answered 0
 and PASSED, because a length read is a load from offset 0 and address 0 is
 mapped and holds zero, so the wrong representation returns the right answer
 by coincidence. Only a row that dereferences the vector fails, and it fails
 at `CR2=fffffffffffffff8` -- the count cell one word below a null pointer.

 `vec-cons` APPENDS, and the order rows below are what pin that. Nothing
 documents these five as a user-facing capability, so the name is the only
 thing suggesting a prepend and it is outvoted: `PunctualProbe.md` records
 `__list_snoc` as the one write primitive behind list-push, list-snoc AND
 vec-cons (Damian, 2026-07-04), which makes `vec-cons` the vector-typed
 sibling of `list-snoc` and the name a wart. A prepend reading would put 1 at
 the head below instead of 2, so these rows fail if anyone changes it.

Section: Subjects

  vs-one : Vector 1 Integer
  vs-one = vec-singleton 7

  vs-two : Vector 2 Integer
  vs-two = vec-cons 1 (vec-singleton 2)

  vs-nil : Vector 0 Integer
  vs-nil = vec-empty

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
   print-line-uni ("vec-length singleton want 1: " & show (vec-length vs-one))
   print-line-uni ("vec-head singleton   want 7: " & show (vec-head vs-one))
   print-line-uni ("vec-length rebuilt    want 1: " & show (vec-length (vec-singleton 42)))
   print-line-uni ("vec-head rebuilt     want 42: " & show (vec-head (vec-singleton 42)))
   print-line-uni ("vec-cons length      want 2: " & show (vec-length vs-two))
   print-line-uni ("vec-cons appends, head stays want 2: " & show (vec-head vs-two))
   print-line-uni ("vec-length empty     want 0: " & show (vec-length vs-nil))
   print-line-uni ("vec-length rebuilt empty want 0: " & show (vec-length vec-empty))
   print-line-uni ("cons onto empty      want 1: " & show (vec-length (vec-cons 5 vec-empty)))
   print-line-uni ("head of that         want 5: " & show (vec-head (vec-cons 5 vec-empty)))
  end
